<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">This
Independent Director Agreement (this &ldquo;<U>Agreement</U>&rdquo;) is made and entered into as of September 8, 2026, by and between
Twenty One Capital, Inc. (the&nbsp;&ldquo;<U>Company</U>&rdquo;), a Texas corporation, and David J. Goldschmidt (the &ldquo;<U>Director</U>&rdquo;).</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: small-caps bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">I.
SERVICES</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: small-caps bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">I.1
<U>Board of Directors</U>. Pursuant to an authorizing resolution of the Company&rsquo;s Board of Directors (the &ldquo;<U>Board</U>&rdquo;),
the Director is appointed to serve as an independent director of the Company&rsquo;s Board, effective as of the date hereof (the &ldquo;<U>Effective
Date</U>&rdquo;), until the date on which the Director ceases to be a member of the Board for any reason (the &ldquo;<U>Expiration Date</U>&rdquo;).
The Director&rsquo;s service as a member of the Board will be subject to (y) applicable law and (z) renomination and reelection by the
shareholders of the Company in accordance with the Company&rsquo;s Amended and Restated Bylaws dated as of May 19, 2026 and other governing
documents (the &ldquo;<U>Organizational Documents</U>&rdquo;). The Director hereby accepts such appointment and agrees to serve as a
Director of the Company, subject to the terms of this Agreement and the Company&rsquo;s Organizational Documents.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">I.2
<U>Director Services</U>. The Director&rsquo;s services to the Company hereunder shall include service on (i) the Board and (ii) any
committee of the Board such Director may be appointed to by the Board, in accordance with applicable law, regulation and stock exchange
rules, and such other services mutually agreed to by the Director and the Company (the &ldquo;<U>Director Services</U>&rdquo;). Notwithstanding
the foregoing the Director shall not serve on more than two committees of the Board at the same time.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: small-caps bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">II.
COMPENSATION</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: small-caps bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">II.1
<U>Expense Reimbursement</U>. The Company shall reimburse the Director for all reasonable travel and other out-of-pocket expenses incurred
in connection with the Director Services rendered by the Director and in accordance with applicable Company policies.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">II.2
<U>Compensation to Director</U>. In consideration for the Director&rsquo;s services under this Agreement (including for the avoidance
of doubt, any services as a member of any committee of the Board), the Company shall pay the Director a cash payment of (i)&nbsp;$150,000
per annum (the &ldquo;<U>Annual Fee</U>&rdquo;) and (ii) $150,000 worth of Class A Stock of the Company per annum (&ldquo;<U>Annual Equity
Award</U>&rdquo;) which shall vest in full upon grant. The Annual Fee shall be paid in equal monthly installments commencing as of the
Effective Date. For the initial period from the Effective Date through the date of the Company's next annual general meeting of shareholders
(the &ldquo;<U>Initial Term</U>&rdquo;), the Annual Fee shall be pro-rated to reflect the portion of the year elapsed during the Initial
Term, and the monthly installment for any partial calendar month shall be further pro-rated accordingly. Thereafter, the monthly installments
of the Annual Fee shall be payable on the first day of each calendar month. The Annual Equity Award shall be granted under the Twenty
One Capital, Inc. 2025 Stock Incentive Plan (the &ldquo;<U>Equity Plan</U>&rdquo;) and on the date of each annual general meeting of
shareholders at which the Director is appointed or reappointed (each such date, a &ldquo;<U>Grant Date</U>&rdquo;) and shall not be subject
to any further vesting conditions. The Annual Equity Award for the Initial Term shall be pro-rated in the same manner as the Annual Fee.
For the Initial Term, the pro-rated Annual Equity Award shall be 15,205 shares of Class A stock of the Company which shall be granted
as soon as practicable following the date hereof.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></P>

